MM: {name:'Martha Mackey', gen:2, line:'valentine', conf:C.p, star:true,
 role:'Bookfolder', dates:'c.1846 – 1900',
 summary:'Married at seventeen and still legally a minor. A bookfolder, so the same trade as her husband. She had eleven children over twenty-six years and died at 54, less than four weeks before my great-grandfather’s wedding.',
 facts:[
 ['Born','c.1846 - possible baptism found, see note'],
 ['Occupation','Bookfolder'],
 ['Married','3 August 1863, St Mary’s Pro-Cathedral, aged 17 (“minor”)'],
 ['Address at marriage','134 Great Britain Street - but see note'],
 ['Religion','Roman Catholic'],
 ['Died','10 July 1900, 30 Portland Place'],
 ['Age at death','54'],
 ['Cause of death','Cardiac asthenia (heart exhaustion)'],
 ['Described as','“Bookbinder’s Wife”']],
 notes:[
 'A baptism of a <b>Martha Herbert</b> in 1846 is the best candidate for her: the year matches her age at death exactly, and the sponsors were Patrick and Catherine Mackey - the same names given as her parents at her wedding. Why the surname is Herbert rather than Mackey is unexplained.',
 'No Martha Mackey was born anywhere in Ireland in the surrounding years, which makes the Herbert record more compelling rather than less.',
 'Her address at the 1863 marriage is recorded as 134 Great Britain Street; the summary chart in the original spreadsheet gives 153 Great Britain Street for that year. The two have not been reconciled.',
 'On her son Thomas’s 1900 marriage record her name is written as Martha <b>Markey</b>, and the 1863 church register uses Markey too - one of several spelling drifts in these documents.'],
 flags:[['probable','Baptism identified as Martha Herbert, 1846 - surname unexplained']],
 sources:[
 ['1846 baptism - possible', IG+'/view/?record_id=c963d01f6e-9829'],
 ['1863 marriage - church record', IG+'/view/?record_id=707108e3c7-312'],
 ['1900 death record', IG+'/view/?record_id=0c9e5f72a2-3909054'],
 ['1900 death certificate (PDF)', IG+'/files/civil/deaths_returns/deaths_1900/05753/4625051.pdf']]},

